<title>UK: UK OUTPUT PRICES UP 0.2% IN JULY.</title>
<headline>UK OUTPUT PRICES UP 0.2% IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in July. (Prev data in brackets)</p>
<p> OUTPUT PRICES (unadj)	   JULY	JUNE    (PREL JUNE)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.2	 -0.2	 (-0.2)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			1.4	 1.1	   (1.1)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 125.2	125.0	(125.0)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    -0.2	-0.2	 (-0.2)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.6	 0.6	   (0.6)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.4	120.6    (120.6)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX-FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    unch	unch	  (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.6	 0.6	   (0.6)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr change		    0.2	 0.2	   (0.3)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr annual rate	     0.9	 0.9	  (1.1)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.5     120.5     (120.6)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
